  "id": "anectine",
  "term": "Anectine",
  "definition": "Anectine is a brand name for succinylcholine chloride, a short-acting muscle relaxant. It works by activating nicotinic receptors at the neuromuscular junction and causing sustained depolarization, which disrupts nerve-to-muscle signaling and leads to brief paralysis of skeletal muscles.",
